🗺️ GitHub Actions — Complete Practical Roadmap
📌 Level 1 — Basics

Simple workflow — hello world
Triggers — push, pull_request, manual (workflow_dispatch)
Jobs — single job, multiple jobs
Steps — run commands, use actions

📌 Level 2 — Real CI Concepts

Matrix strategy — multiple versions parallel (jo tune dekha)
Caching — pip/npm cache for faster builds
Artifacts — upload/download between jobs
Environment variables & secrets
Conditional steps — if: conditions

📌 Level 3 — Multi-Job Workflows

Job dependencies — needs: keyword
Sequential jobs — build → test → deploy order
Parallel jobs
Reusable workflows — workflow_call

📌 Level 4 — CD Concepts

Docker build & push to Docker Hub / ECR
GitHub Environments — dev/staging/prod
Deployment with approvals — manual gate
Deploy to EC2 / EKS

📌 Level 5 — Advanced

Self-hosted runners
OIDC — AWS authentication (no hardcoded keys)
SonarQube integration
Security scanning — Trivy, Snyk
Notifications — Slack/email on failure



